423 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 330 0 R
/T (Because pathways organize the entire student experience, how students enter and move through them matters. Before committing, students explore pathways through application and recruitment, introductory experiences, and early career-awareness activities such as industry tours and panels. Students formally select a pathway as they enter the program in 11th grade and commit to that single pathway for two years, because depth is what makes the model work: sequenced projects, credentials, and a coordinated work-based learning progression. Students still encounter adjacent fields through cross-pathway showcases, shared professional-skills instruction, and industry events.)
/E (Because pathways organize the entire student experience, how students enter and move through them matters. Before committing, students explore pathways through application and recruitment, introductory experiences, and early career-awareness activities such as industry tours and panels. Students formally select a pathway as they enter the program in 11th grade and commit to that single pathway for two years, because depth is what makes the model work: sequenced projects, credentials, and a coordinated work-based learning progression. Students still encounter adjacent fields through cross-pathway showcases, shared professional-skills instruction, and industry events.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
