/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 332 0 R
/T (Project-Based Learning \(PBL\) is how students learn the work through teacher-facilitated, standards- and credential-aligned projects in STEAM classrooms and labs. Work-Based Learning \(WBL\) is where students do the work, applying those skills in authentic industry settings through job shadows, mentorships, internships, and paid placements. The two are intentionally sequenced: PBL builds skills, WBL tests them in real-world settings, and those experiences strengthen future learning.)
/E (Project-Based Learning \(PBL\) is how students learn the work through teacher-facilitated, standards- and credential-aligned projects in STEAM classrooms and labs. Work-Based Learning \(WBL\) is where students do the work, applying those skills in authentic industry settings through job shadows, mentorships, internships, and paid placements. The two are intentionally sequenced: PBL builds skills, WBL tests them in real-world settings, and those experiences strengthen future learning.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
