2019 0 obj
<<
/Title (Career pathways anchor curriculum and instruction to authentic fields such as healthcare, technology, engineering, or creative industries. The specific pathways vary by school and region, but the model always aligns projects, skill development, credentials, and work-based learning within each pathway.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1844 0 R
/Next 2020 0 R
>>
endobj
2020 0 obj
<<
/Title (Because pathways organize the entire student experience, how students enter and move through them matters. Before committing, students explore pathways through application and recruitment, introductory experiences, and early career-awareness activities such as industry tours and panels. Students formally select a pathway as they enter the program in 11th grade and commit to that single pathway for two years, because depth is what makes the model work: sequenced projects, credentials, and a coordinated work-based learning progression. Students still encounter adjacent fields through cross-pathway showcases, shared professional-skills instruction, and industry events.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1844 0 R
/Prev 2019 0 R
>>
endobj
